With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

OF SOUTH TANGERANG CITY

And

MAYOR OF SOUTH TANGERANG

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SOUTH TANGERANG CITY CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 5

The protection and service activities for victims as referred to in Article 3, include:
a. Health services;
b. Victim assistance;
c. Counseling;
d. Spiritual guidance;
e. Resocialization; and
f. Empowerment.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

Article 6

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to:
a. Protection;
b. Obtain information;
c. Optimal services;
d. Continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage;
e. Confidential handling;
f. Psychological and legal assistance;
g. Guarantee of rights related to status as a family member or community member.

CHAPTER IV

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 7

1. The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to carry out prevention and mitigation efforts against the occurrence of violence against women and children.
2. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1), are implemented in the form of:
a. Collecting data and information about women and child victims of violence;
b. Conducting education on anti-violence values against women and children;
c. Socializing laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and child victims of violence;
d. Training for PPT members;
e. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and child victims of violence.
3. To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government is obliged to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving relevant community elements;
b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
